---
// Home page sections below the hero (spec section 6, items 3 to 9).
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../../assets/dennis-mccarthy.png';
import { curriculum } from '../../lib/curriculum';
import { url, YOUTUBE_URL } from '../../lib/url';
import PathCard from '../PathCard.astro';
import PipelineMap from '../PipelineMap.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../ProjectCard.astro';
---

<div class="home not-content">
	<section class="band ai" aria-labelledby="ai">
		<div class="inner narrow">
			<h2 id="ai">Is DevOps still worth learning now AI writes code?</h2>
			<p>
				<strong>Yes.</strong> AI can write code, but someone still has to build it, test it, ship it, secure it and
				keep it running. AI means more code arrives, faster. That makes reliable pipelines, infrastructure as code and
				good monitoring matter more, not less.
			</p>
			<p><a href={url('/reference/faq/#is-devops-still-worth-learning-now-ai-writes-code')}>Read the full answer</a></p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band" aria-labelledby="big-picture">
		<div class="inner">
			<h2 id="big-picture">Every track teaches one stage of the same pipeline</h2>
			<p class="intro">
				A change starts as code and ends up running in production, watched by monitoring. Each line on the map covers
				one stretch of that journey.
			</p>
			<PipelineMap interactive />
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band alt" aria-labelledby="ways-in">
		<div class="inner">
			<h2 id="ways-in">Pick a path, or just pick a unit</h2>
			<p class="intro">A path is a route across the map. The coloured strip shows which lines it travels on.</p>
			<div class="ld-grid">
				{curriculum.paths.map((p) => <PathCard path={p} />)}
			</div>
			<p class="more"><a href={url('/curriculum/')}>See every unit</a></p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band" aria-labelledby="how">
		<div class="inner">
			<h2 id="how">How every unit works</h2>
			<ol class="steps">
				<li>
					<h3>Read</h3>
					<p>A short lesson that explains the why.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<h3>Do</h3>
					<p>A hands-on lab from a ready-made starting point.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<h3>Check</h3>
					<p>A script tells you whether it worked.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<h3>Watch</h3>
					<p>Videos on the <a href={YOUTUBE_URL}>London IAC YouTube channel</a>, where available.</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band alt" aria-labelledby="projects">
		<div class="inner">
			<h2 id="projects">What you'll build</h2>
			<p class="intro">Five projects join the units together, from a small fleet of Linux servers to production on AWS and Kubernetes.</p>
			<div class="ld-grid">
				{curriculum.projects.map((p, i) => <ProjectCard project={p} number={i + 1} />)}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band" aria-labelledby="teacher">
		<div class="inner teacher">
			<Image
				class="photo"
				src={portrait}
				alt="Dennis McCarthy"
				width={288}
				height={288}
				widths={[144, 288]}
				sizes="9rem"
				loading="lazy"
			/>
			<div>
				<h2 id="teacher">Who's teaching</h2>
				<p class="name">Dennis McCarthy</p>
				<p>
					I've spent 20 years automating Linux systems, and I run the London Infrastructure as Code meetup. From shell
					scripts to CI/CD pipelines and AI coding, I've seen a lot along the way.
				</p>
				<p class="more-about"><a href={url('/about/')}>More about the course</a></p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band cta" aria-labelledby="ready">
		<div class="inner narrow">
			<h2 id="ready">Ready? Unit L1 runs right here in your browser.</h2>
			<a class="ld-button" href={url('/units/l1/')}>Start unit L1</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</div>

<style>
	.home {
		margin-inline: calc(-1 * var(--sl-content-pad-x));
	}
	.band {
		padding: 4rem var(--sl-content-pad-x);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--ld-border);
	}
	.band.alt {
		background: var(--ld-bg-alt);
	}
	.inner {
		max-width: var(--ld-max);
		margin: 0 auto;
	}
	.inner.narrow {
		max-width: 44rem;
	}
	h2 {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-h2);
		font-weight: 800;
		line-height: 1.1;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}
	.intro {
		max-width: 44rem;
		margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
		color: var(--ld-muted);
		font-size: 1.125rem;
	}
	.ai p {
		font-size: 1.1875rem;
	}
	.ai p + p {
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}
	.more {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}
	/* Read, Do, Check, Watch is a real sequence, so it reads left to right
	   along a rail, like stops on a line. */
	.steps {
		position: relative;
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.5rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
		counter-reset: step;
	}
	@media (min-width: 50rem) {
		.steps {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
		}
		.steps::before {
			content: '';
			position: absolute;
			top: 0.75rem;
			left: 0.75rem;
			right: 12%;
			height: var(--ld-rail);
			margin-top: calc(var(--ld-rail) / -2);
			border-radius: 3px;
			background: var(--ld-accent);
		}
	}
	.steps li {
		position: relative;
		padding-top: 2.25rem;
	}
	.steps li::before {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		top: 0;
		left: 0;
		width: 1.5rem;
		height: 1.5rem;
		border: 4px solid var(--ld-accent);
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--ld-bg);
	}
	.steps h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
		font-size: 1.375rem;
	}
	.steps p {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--ld-muted);
	}
	.teacher {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 2rem;
		align-items: center;
	}
	.teacher h2 {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	.name {
		margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--ld-heading);
	}
	.photo {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		width: 9rem;
		height: 9rem;
		object-fit: contain;
	}
	.more-about {
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
	}
	.cta {
		text-align: center;
	}
	.cta h2 {
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}
</style>
